•fauthorxApub:sha2-256:srsdpdvxotuqshmlmmio73gcwcg7ynjbnub64lujp3z5kkqeuycadbodyßeclassharchivalgcontentxwintegrations 0.17.0 was released on 2026-11-26 from commit 4afc2272dec5b5a91d94976072f39f800d9a3193 with these changes.ddata¢gcolumnsÇ°dnamehcategory°dnamefchangedrowsïÇgchangedxŒThe ingest pod no longer writes its report of each pass as a file into the project's buffer: it goes with that project's next reports job, or as a job of its own once none has gone for INGEST_REPORT_SECONDSÇeaddedy£The ingest pod takes storage's signed notices of files in a buffer's inbox (POST /ingest/notify, HMAC-SHA256 with INGEST_NOTIFY_KEY over the timestamp and body; refused without the key) and loads the named files without listing, a buffer's batches at least INGEST_BATCH_GAP_SECONDS apart; INGEST_SWEEP_SECONDS and INGEST_REPORT_SECONDS set how often it lists every buffer and loads its own reports (120 each, as before)ÇeaddedyA sender can write only when it has calls to send: with CALL_LOG_DEADLINE_SECONDS (StorageSink's deadline_seconds; in JS deadlineSeconds and flushDue(); the call-log object's vars), each dataset's file goes once its first unsent call has waited the deadline, and no report goes alone, the counters riding in the next call file; with CALL_LOG_HEARTBEAT_SECONDS too, a quiet dataset also writes its report alone each heartbeat (a heartbeat alone has a deadline of two minutes); with neither set, a file every two minutes as beforeÇeaddedx¥The call-log object tells the ingest pod of each file R2 takes, signed with its secret INGEST_NOTIFY_KEY (caller.js's notifyIngest and noticeSignature), and tells no one without itÇgchangedy@With CALL_LOG_DEADLINE_SECONDS set and CALL_LOG_HEARTBEAT_SECONDS not, a sender (StorageSink, caller.js's StorageSink, the call-log object) writes no report-only files: a file only when it has calls, the counters riding in the next; a heartbeat alone keeps a two-minute deadline, and neither set a file every two minutesÇgchangedxçGoogleToken, FederatedToken and google_token take the scope and the plugin operation their calls are recorded as (BigQuery's load by default)Çeaddedy™integrations.heartbeat: with CALL_LOG_METRIC_SECONDS, StorageSink writes each instance's heartbeat to Cloud Monitoring (custom.googleapis.com/sustenaut/heartbeat on global, labels project, sender and instance) through the Caller as google.monitoring write, with the Google credential CALL_LOG_METRIC_CREDENTIAL_FILE or GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS names; unset, nothing is written; the google.monitoring plugin is registeredÇgchangedxùA Caller given no clock, sleep or random looks them up at each call; use_clock() (useClock() in JS) sets them for a harness, reaching a Caller made before itÇeaddedx≤cassette_reports() (cassetteReports() in JS) and Cassette.report(): what each cassette current_transport() made answered, for a harness's exit report in place of reading _by_modeÇeaddedx©`Given someone else pushes to "BRANCH" of "o/r":` makes a real commit on the branch when recording, which the code under test meets as a race, and does nothing replayingÇeaddedx˙INTEGRATIONS_FAULTS, a JSON list of Faulty's rules, puts the transport current_transport() gives a process under them, so a harness's faults reach the programs it runs; a fault's plugin also covers every plugin under it, before a dot (both languages)ÇeaddedxÊ`integrations test-org sweep` deletes the GitHub test org's rec-* repositories older than a day (--older-than-hours), and the test-org workflow runs it daily; github.repo-ops has the test-org and test-org-sweep operations for themÇeaddedxëRecorder(names=...) (both languages) and INTEGRATIONS_NAMES write each real name a recording meets as the scenario's, wherever it is a whole wordÇeaddedyRecording, `Given the GitHub repository "o/r" holds:` (integrations.testing.github) makes a private rec-<consumer>-<run>-<n> repository in the GitHub test org (INTEGRATIONS_TEST_ORG, else SustenautTest) holding exactly its files, with the recorder app's credentials (GITHUB_TEST_RECORDER_APP_ID, _APP_KEY and _INSTALLATION_ID, or GITHUB_TEST_RECORDER_TOKEN), puts its real names in INTEGRATIONS_NAMES so the cassette says o/r, and deletes it when the scenario ends; token(ctx) is the token the code under test calls withÇgchangedyReplaying, a placeholder first seen in a request binds to the first value of its kind the code sends there, and is that value from then on: answered as it, where before a stand-in, and only it matches again; a value already another placeholder's matches none (both languages)Çeaddedxò@sustenaut/integrations/testing/github.js: GitHub's test steps for Node, the test customer `github` for pubtest's register(api, { customers: [github] })ÇeaddedyA Recorder name may be a label, ‚ü¶integrations:commit:L‚üß: applied before the volatile patterns, so a labelled sha is written as its label, kept in the cassette's map, replayed as itself, and matched when the code sends it back, in a URL percent-encoded or not (both languages)ÇgchangedxæA test org repository's name has a part of its process's own, rec-<consumer>-<run>-<process>-<n>, so parallel workers never pick the same one; nothing else in the test org may be named rec-*Çeaddedy_GitHub's test steps label commits: the holds step's commit is "start" (a later repository's "start-<name>"), `Given someone else pushes to "BRANCH" of "o/r" as commit "L":` labels its own, and commit(ctx, "o/r", "L") (both languages) is the real sha recording and ‚ü¶integrations:commit:L‚üß replaying; a label taken, not a word, or unknown is refusedÇefixedxúThe wait for a new test org repository's first branch sleeps with its Caller's sleep, which a harness's use_clock() reaches, not time.sleep (both languages)Çeaddedy6pubrules.json's variables block is version 2 and gives INGEST_SWEEP_SECONDS, INGEST_REPORT_SECONDS and INGEST_BATCH_GAP_SECONDS the default "120", the code's constant, so the deploy walk (pubdeploy 0.8.1, pubsec 0.4.0) finds them ready unset; a scenario holds each default to the constant and reads "" as unsetgdependsÅxApub:sha2-256:vj7rqc26m7ubcf5mtfzjkiz4vhcxpu7z5tsiv4lb4tnw3lbu7w2ahevidenceÅ§dkindhexternalcreflintegrationshrevisionx(4afc2272dec5b5a91d94976072f39f800d9a3193drolefsourcedlangbenescope¢jconditionsÄfdomainx-the published release v0.17.0 of integrationsgcreatedt2026-11-26T00:00:00Zcpuba1dtypekclaim.prose